# Whitespace rules per file kind.
#
# Markdown uses **two trailing spaces** as a hard line break — that is a
# rendering feature of CommonMark, not stray whitespace, and deleting the two
# spaces would change what the document renders as. `git diff --check` would
# otherwise report every one of them as "trailing whitespace", so the check
# has to be taught the difference.
#
# Only Markdown is exempted: every other file kind keeps the default rules
# (blank at end of line, blank at end of file, space before tab), so real
# trailing whitespace is still reported everywhere else.
*.md whitespace=-blank-at-eol
